    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0353" n="1107" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1107"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-28T20:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 28, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.28 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8085. My telegram 8014, December 20, 9 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d233-f1"/>
                    British are prepared to grant article 1 Swedish <hi rendition="#italic">modus
                        vivendi</hi> and release of the 22,000 bags of coffee mentioned in article
                    6. But [<hi rendition="#italic">And?</hi>] they will approve the request for
                    permission to import an additional 50,000 bags. Articles 7 and 8 are under
                    consideration. Present difficulties which could only be surmounted by proper
                    safeguards especially in regard to the leather which might be used by the Swedes
                    for manufacture of boots for Germany or release equivalent quantity, and the
                    cork bricks which would be used for storing meat which might subsequently be
                    released to the enemy.</p>
                <p>It is desirable that the other requirements in the Swedish <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> be met. Nothing prevents fullest
                    extent possible in order that a tonnage <hi rendition="#italic">modus
                        vivendi</hi> may be put promptly into operation. The negotiations are in
                    abeyance pending our decisions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
